+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+/*
+ * Allwinner A733 (sun60iw2) KMS -- the drm_device this pixel path never had.
+ *
+ * Every block on the way from DRAM to the monitor is already driver code in
+ * this tree and eleven of the fourteen patches that got them there are proven
+ * on silicon: the AUX channel and the EDID it reads (`drm-allwinner-a733-displayport-aux` and an earlier EDID patch not carried here), the main-link
+ * PHY (`drm-a733-dp-configure-the-main-link-phy`), TCON_TV1's raster (`drm-a733-tcon-tv1-timing-generator-and-video-source`), the DisplayPort video stream (`drm-a733-dp-the-main-video-stream`),
+ * link training (`drm-a733-dp-link-training`) and the display engine that pulls pixels out of DRAM
+ * (`drm-a733-display-engine-dram-into-tcon-tv1`, first pixels on 2026-08-19). What has never existed is the object that
+ * ties them together: no drm_device binds on this SoC, so drm_client_setup() is
+ * never called, there is no /dev/fb0 and nothing above these drivers can ask
+ * for a mode. Everything they do is reached through debugfs by hand.
+ *
+ * This file is that object, and nothing more than that object -- one CRTC on
+ * TCON_TV1, one plane out of one display-engine channel, one encoder, and the
+ * connector `drm-a733-dp-register-a-drm-bridge`'s bridge hangs on.
+ *
+ * WHAT IS PROVEN AND WHAT IS NOT, because a green build is not proof:
+ *
+ *   ⬜ NOTHING IN THIS FILE HAS RUN ON SILICON. It applies and it compiles, and
+ *      that is the whole of the claim. The blocks underneath it are proven; the
+ *      frame around them is not, and the two are different statements.
+ *   ⬜ The observable that closes it is a framebuffer test,
+ *      namely: /dev/fb0 at 1920x1200; a known pattern written into it is
+ *      on the screen; the same pattern read back and compared with cmp matches.
+ *      Falsified by: no /dev/fb0; a cmp mismatch; or a screen that does not
+ *      change when the buffer changes.
+ *   ⬜ VBLANK IS NOT WIRED. TCON_TV1's interrupt (INTID 90 = GIC SPI 58) is in
+ *      the device tree and nothing requests it, so drm_vblank_init() is
+ *      deliberately NOT called -- see the block above sun60i_kms_bind().
