+ * ⚠ THE SINGLE LOAD-BEARING LINE IN THIS FILE IS `.fb_create =
+ * drm_gem_fb_create`, NOT drm_gem_fb_create_with_dirty. That choice IS the
+ * proof above. drm_fbdev_dma_driver_fbdev_probe() branches on
+ * `fb->funcs->dirty` (drm_fbdev_dma.c:315): with a .dirty callback the fbdev
+ * client allocates a SHADOW buffer and defers copies into the real scanout
+ * buffer, so /dev/fb0 is not the memory the display engine fetches. Reading it
+ * back would then compare a shadow with itself, and a poke into it would not
+ * reach the screen without a flush -- the two halves of that falsifier,
+ * both silently defeated. _with_dirty exists for hardware that needs damage
+ * tracking; this one scans DRAM continuously and needs none.
+ *
