+ *      The vendor writes the blender output attributes straight to MMIO in the
+ *      middle of an otherwise queue-based commit, and says why:
+ *      "rtmx en & tcon en & bld disable (rcq copy needs to wait until the next
+ *      plane update) which will cause tcon to think that de is enabled, but bld
+ *      has no output, resulting in missing data" (sunxi_de.c:852-858).
+ *      ⇒ Here the constraint is met by ORDER alone and no special case is
+ *      needed: `drm-a733-display-engine-dram-into-tcon-tv1` commits by direct CPU store, so sun60i_de_blender()'s
